BY ARM -- and why the arms must NOT be compared on this outcome
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  mode 3 = repository DECLARED dependencies, they were installed
  mode 5 = repository declared NOTHING, executed in an anaconda base env

  mode      n   finished  same  same&real   exception-rows  of those count=0
   3     2365     150     150        0            630            626
   5     2308     246      95       35           1635            395

  A row that raised a CELL execution error must have run a cell. In mode 3
  such rows have count=0 almost always, so `count` is not a faithful record
  of cells executed in that arm -- the tracker does not advance there. That
  does NOT weaken the correction above (the loop bound is the same variable,
  so nothing was compared either way) but it does mean the declared-vs-not
  comparison on this outcome measures the instrumentation, not the world.
